      "content": "Figure 1, the proposed system architecture. Two inputs enter on the left as document shapes: \"Business Process Modelling Notation (BPMN) XML — Multi-step workflow\" and \"API Specifications — 20+ endpoints\". Five numbered boxes follow, each split into what the LLM does (white) and what it emits (tinted). Step 1, Workflow Breakdown: the LLM agent extracts sequential steps, output \"Structured Steps with conditions\", the box giving as its example \"Step 2 ---> Step 3 / If True ---> Step 5\". Step 2, Create API Service: the LLM generates a Python wrapper class, output \"service.py — Class with methods per endpoint\". Steps 1 and 2 both feed Step 3, Tool/Context: the LLM generates async tools plus context, output \"tools.py — async functions, Tool context class\". Step 4, Agent Prompt: the LLM creates structured instructions, output \"{agent_prompt}.md — Workflow logic map, Tool usage rules\". Step 5, Execution Wrapper: the LLM adapts a FastAPI template, output \"agent.py — Rest API service\". The final box, shaded green, reads \"Final Output: Deployable — Complete agent system, API Service + Tools, Prompt + Wrapper\". The flow is strictly forward; no arrow returns to an earlier step, so the iterative refinement the text describes in step 4 of §3.3 is not drawn here.",
